Whereas, although President Dr. Mohamed Muizzu, speaking at the official ceremony held on the occasion of the Maldives' Independence Day on 26 July 2024, said that Rasmale is "land that will never be sold to any foreign party or given away free";

Whereas it has been agreed to give the area of the larger part of the 500 hectares of land reclaimed in Rasmale to the Eagle Hills company for a period of 99 years;

Whereas, under Article 70(c)(3) of the Constitution of the Republic of Maldives, this Majlis is charged with the responsibility of [unclear] overseeing the governance of the land and holding the use of the land accountable, and of taking measures in accordance with the Constitution and laws to do these things;

I submit this resolution calling on the Government to disclose the agreement relating to the 'Maldives Waterfront and Marina' project to run a project in Rasmale, and to determine the views of the Members of the People's Majlis on this matter.

Submitting Member: Member for Galolhu Dhekunu constituency, Meekail Ahmed Nasym
Signature: [signature]
Date: 11 October 2026
